# What `docker build .` should not have to send.
#
# Without this the build context is about 145 MB, nearly all of it `target/` —
# a compiled tree the image cannot use anyway, since stage 1 builds from source
# inside the image and the host's artifacts are for a different platform. The
# context that actually matters is around 2 MB.
#
# Everything the Dockerfile COPYs must stay out of this file: Cargo.toml,
# Cargo.lock, rust-toolchain.toml, crates/, test/, tests/, scripts/,
# fuzz/reference/, package.json, Makefile, DECISIONS.md, README.md,
# .port-mortem.toml.

target/
.git/
node_modules/

# The host's build of the addon. Stage 1 produces the one the image runs, and
# shipping a Windows or macOS artifact into a Linux image would at best be
# ignored and at worst be confusing.
decimal.node

# Harness inputs and outputs that no build step reads.
fuzz/log.txt
fuzz/log-limits.txt
bench/
docs/
